<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Poppo of Frisia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 734</span> · Also known as Bubo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Poppo, also called Bubo, was a king of the Frisians in the early 8th century, probably the successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redbad">Redbad</a>. A pagan, he resisted Frankish expansion and Christian missions until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> in 734 and defeated and killed him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-boarn">Battle of the Boarn</a>. His death ended the independent Frisian kingdom.</p></div>
